      "output": {
        "message": "Here are three practical ways to handle this: 1. **Clarify priority right away.** When a late task arrives, send a brief reply: *\"Got it. I'm heading out for the day—is this urgent for tonight, or should I tackle it first thing tomorrow morning?\"* This sets a boundary without ignoring the request, and most of the time it isn't actually an emergency.\n2. **Do a quick end-of-day check-in.** About 30 minutes before you leave, ask your supervisor if there is anything time-sensitive needed before tomorrow. That can prompt them to send tasks earlier rather than right as you are walking out.\n3. **Bring it up in a one-on-one.** If it keeps happening, address the pattern when you aren't in the middle of it. You can explain that receiving new assignments at the very end of the day makes it hard to plan your workload, and ask how they prefer to handle evening tasks versus next-morning priorities.",
